nftconf (1.3.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * One config statement maps to one live nft rule by default so later
    edits/shrinks still unload. load -c/--compact packs matching
    statements into nft sets (previous behaviour).
  * unload removes a statement only when the whole live rule matches;
    unload -f/--force splits a compacted leftover and removes as many
    atoms as possible.
  * show is no longer an alias of check: it prints each statement with
    a width-8 status (on, N/M, ---, xxx).
  * Same-line # comments on a statement (allow incoming tcp 1234 # note)
    are copied into the nft rule comment after the ownership tag.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:15:29 +0800

nftconf (1.2.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * Refactor filter policy to allow/deny with incoming and outgoing:
    allow incoming tcp PORT..., deny incoming udp PORT...,
    allow outgoing ip CIDR [tcp/udp PORT...].
  * Omit the port part on outgoing to match all traffic to that CIDR.
  * Resolve overlaps by specificity: a single port beats a range; at the
    same specificity, allow beats deny (nftables first-match order).
  * whitelist/blacklist remain aliases for allow/deny incoming.
  * Add OUTPUT filter chains for outgoing policy.
  * Docker lab: function-cover tests for allow/deny incoming and outgoing
    (port vs range, CIDR deny, longer prefix) plus NAT/shield/daemon/pidfile.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:51:00 +0800

nftconf (1.1.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * TCP/UDP (also sctp/dccp) port specs accept a port, an inclusive range,
    or a space/comma-separated list, e.g. whitelist tcp 80 443 1080 8000-8080.
    Multiple atoms become one nftables anonymous set; a single atom stays
    a scalar. The same forms work on nat/dnat/snat/masquerade/redirect
    before "to".
  * Reject inverted ranges and ports outside 0–65535; normalize leading
    zeros. ADDR:PORT on the first item applies to following bare ports.
  * reject … with TYPE keeps every token after "with" (e.g. tcp reset).
  * convert expands list dports into $whitelist_ports / $app_ports.
  * Document the configuration language in full: info manual
    (docs/nftconf.adoc), guide.md, nftconf(1) and localized man pages,
    README examples, and demo whitelist comments.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:30:16 +0800

nftconf (1.0.1) testing; urgency=medium

  * Fix /usr/bin/nftconf ModuleNotFoundError for nftconf_app:
    use #!/usr/bin/python3 and bootstrap sys.path to dist-packages
    when a non-system python3 is first on PATH.

